5740 0 obj
<</A 23155 0 R /Alt(Figure 4.12: Internal design of an 8 to 3 encoder. There are four OR gates. The first has inputs I4, I5, I6, and I7 and output O2. The second has inputs I2, I3, I6, and I7 and output O1. The third has inputs I1, I3, I5, and I7 and output O0. The last has inputs I0 to I7 and output V.␀)/K 12/P 31 0 R /Pg 15303 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
5741 0 obj
<</A 23156 0 R /Alt(Figure 4.12: Internal design of an 8 to 3 encoder. There are four OR gates. The first has inputs I4, I5, I6, and I7 and output O2. The second has inputs I2, I3, I6, and I7 and output O1. The third has inputs I1, I3, I5, and I7 and output O0. The last has inputs I0 to I7 and output V.␀)/K 13/P 31 0 R /Pg 15303 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
5742 0 obj
<</A 23159 0 R /Alt(Figure 4.13: 8 to 3 priority encoder: \(a\) Truth table; \(b\) Circuit design. The portions of the circuit that generate O2 and V are the same as in the previous figure. The circuit to generate O1 has a two 2-input OR gate with inputs I2 and I3, and a 2-input NOR gate with inputs I4 and I5. the outputs of these two gates are input to a 2-input AND gate. The output of that gate, and I6 and I7, are input to a 3-input OR gate with output O1. The circuit to generate O0 has three AND gates with inputs I2 passed through a NOT gate, I4 passed through a NOT gate, I6 passed through a NOT gate, and I1; I4 passed through a NOT gate, I6 passed through a NOT gate, and I3; and I6 passed through a NOT gate and I5. The outputs of these three gates, and I7, are input to a 4-input OR gate with output O0.␀)/K 0/P 31 0 R /Pg 15304 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
