6093 0 obj
<</A 23174 0 R /Alt(Figure 4.15: \(a\) 16 to 1 multiplexer constructed using two 8 to 1 multiplexers; \(b\) Truth table.  The circuit has two 8 to 1 multiplexers with inputs I0 to I7 and I8 to I15. The select inputs of each multiplexer are connected to inputs S2, S1, and S0. The enable signal of the upper multiplexer is connected to S3 passed through an inverter. The enable signal of the lower multiplexer is connected to S3. The output of each multiplexer is connected to a 2-input OR gate with output O0.␀)/K 155/P 31 0 R /Pg 15307 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
6094 0 obj
<</K[ 6086 0 R  156]/P 31 0 R /Pg 15307 0 R /S/P>>
endobj
6095 0 obj
<</A 23175 0 R /Alt(Figure 4.16: 8 to 1 multiplexer \(a\) Truth table; \(b\) Internal design. There are eight 4-input AND gates, each of which has one of eight possible combinations of a or a', b or b', c or c', and the input I0 to I7 corresponding to the value of a, b, and c. The outputs of these gates are connected to two 4-input OR gates. The outputs of these two gates are input to a 2-input OR gate with output O0.␀)/K 0/P 31 0 R /Pg 15308 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
