6719 0 obj
<</A 23225 0 R /Alt(Figure 4.22: \(a\) An enhanced 1-bit comparator; \(b\) Four-bit comparator. The circuit in Figure a has two 2-input OR gates. The first OR gate has inputs A>Bin and the output of an AND gate with inputs A=Bin, A, and B passed through an inverter; its output is A>Bout. The second OR gate has inputs A<Bin and the output of an AND gate with inputs A=Bin, B, and A passed through an inverter; its output is A<Bout. A 2-input NOR gate has A>Bout and B>Aout as its inputs and A=Bout as its output. In b, four comparators are cascaded, with inputs A3 and B3, A2 and B2, A1 and B1, and A0 and B0. The inputs of the first comparator are A>Bin=0, A=Bin=1, and A<Bin=0. The outputs of each comparator are input to the next comparator. The outputs of the final comparator are A>B, A=B, and A<B.␀)/K 0/P 31 0 R /Pg 15083 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
