<</A 21957 0 R /Alt(Figure 6.22: Internal design of the positive edge-triggered J-K flip-flop with preset and clear. The circuit has two 3-input NAND gates, four 3-input AND gates, and two 2-input NOR gates. The first NAND gate has inputs CLR', J, and CLK passed through a NOT gate. The second NAND gate has inputs PRE', K, and CLK passed through a NOT gate. The first AND gate has inputs PRE', the output of the first NAND gate, and the output of the second NOR gate. The second AND gate has inputs PRE',  CLK passed through a NOT gate, and the output of the second NOR gate. The third AND gate has inputs CLR', CLK passed through a NOT gate, and the output of the first NOR gate. The fourth AND gate has inputs CLR', the output of the second NAND gate, and the output of the first NOR gate. The first NOR gate has the outputs of the first two AND gates as its inputs and Q as its output. The second NOR gate has the outputs of the third and fourth AND gates as its inputs and Q' as its output.␀)/K 63/P 34 0 R /Pg 14493 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
9319 0 obj
<</A 21945 0 R /Alt(Figure 6.21: Creating a J-K flip-flop using a D flip-flop: \(a\) Excitation table; \(b\) Karnaugh map to generate D; \(c\) Final circuit. The final circuit is a D flip-flop with input D connected to the output of a 2-input OR gate. The inputs of the OR gate are connected to two 2-input AND gates. The first AND gate has inputs J and output Q' of the flip-flop. The inputs to the second AND gate are connected to K passed through a NOT gate and output Q of the flip-flop. Outputs Q and Q' of the flip-flop are labeled Q and Q', respectively.␀)/K 64/P 34 0 R /Pg 14493 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
