<</A 18595 0 R /Alt(Figure 7.21: 4-bit synchronous upcounter. The circuit has four D flip-flops, each receiving its clock input from a 2-input AND gate with inputs COUNT and CLK. The D input of the least significant bit is its Q' output. The D input of the next flip-flop is the XOR of its Q output and the Q output of the previous flip-flop. The D input of the next flip-flop is the XOR of its Q output and the output of an 2-input AND gate which has the Q outputs of the first two flip-flops as its inputs. The D input of the last flip-flop is the XOR of its Q input and the output of a 2-input AND gate which has the output of the previous AND gate and the Q output of the previous flip-flop as its inputs.␀)/K 13/P 35 0 R /Pg 14499 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
