<</A 19968 0 R /Alt(Figure 8.23 Combinatorial logic circuits to generate the next state and output for the Moore machine. The circuit to generate NS1 has two AND gates with inputs PS1 and PS0 passed through a NOT gate, and PS1 passed through a NOT gate, PS0, and I. The outputs of the AND gates are input to an OR gate that outputs NS1. The circuit to generate NS0 has three AND gates with inputs PS1 passed through a NOT gate, PS0, and I passed through a NOT gate; PS1 and I; and PS0 passed through a NOT gate and I. The outputs are input to an OR gate that outputs NS0. The circuit to generate O is a single 2-input AND gate with inputs PS1 and PS0 and output O.␀)/K 12/P 36 0 R /Pg 19302 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
