<</A 20158 0 R /Alt(Figure 8.48: Partial timing diagram for the 1s counter. The diagram has signals CLK, PS1, PS0, and I. Initially, CLK=0, PS1=1, PS0=0, and I is pulsed from 0 to 1 to 0 twice. Then CLK changes to 1. The other signals are not shown once this transition occurs.␀)/K 15/P 36 0 R /Pg 19098 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
12575 0 obj
<</A 20159 0 R /Alt(Figure 8.49: Completed timing diagram for the 1s counter. This expands the previous partial diagram by adding signals NS1, NS0, and O. NS1 is alway the complement of I. NS0 is always 0. O is the same as I. PS1, PS0, and I retain their previous values once CLK changes to 1.␀)/K 16/P 36 0 R /Pg 19098 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
