12588 0 obj
<</A 20160 0 R /Alt(Figure 8.50: Circuit implementing the Mealy machine for the 1s counter with flip-flop for output O. The circuit has three D flip-flops labeled PS1, PS0, and O. All flip-flops have CLK connected to their clock inputs. The D input to PS1 is labeled NS1. It is the output of a 2-input OR gate with inputs connected to the outputs of 2-input AND gates. The first AND gate has inputs connected to the Q output of the PS0 flip-flop and I, and the second AND gate has inputs connected to the Q output of the PS1 flip-flop and I passed through a NOT gate. The D input to PS0 is labeled NS0. It is the output of a 2-input OR gate with inputs connected to the outputs of a 2-input AND gate and a 3-input AND gate. The first AND gate has inputs connected to the Q output of the PS0 flip-flop and I passed through a NOT gate, and the second AND gate has inputs connected to the Q' output of the PS1 flip-flop, the Q' output of the PS0 flip-flop, and I. The input to the O flip-flop is connected to a 2-input AND gate with inputs connected to the Q output of the PS1 flip-flop and I.␀)/K 11/P 36 0 R /Pg 19099 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
