<</A 20183 0 R /Alt(Exercise 8.12: The circuit has three D flip-flops labeled PS1, PS0, and O. All flip-flops have CLK connected to their clock inputs. The D input to PS1 is labeled NS1. It is the output of a 2-input OR gate with inputs connected to the outputs of 3-input AND gates. The first AND gate has inputs connected to the Q' output of the PS1 flip-flop, the Q output of the PS0 flip-flop,  and I, and the second AND gate has inputs connected to the Q output of the PS1 flip-flop, the Q' output of the PS0 flip-flop,  and I. The D input to PS0 is labeled NS0. It is the output of a 2-input OR gate with one input connected to I passed through a NOT gate and the other input connected to the output of a 2-input AND gate  with inputs connected to the Q output of the PS1 flip-flop and the Q' output of the PS0 flip-flop. The input to the O flip-flop is connected to a 2-input AND gate with inputs connected to the Q output of the PS1 flip-flop and the Q output of the PS0 flip-flop.␀)/K 37/P 36 0 R /Pg 19102 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
