<</A 26119 0 R /Alt(Figure 9.29: \(a\) Circuit with a dynamic hazard, and \(b\) its timing diagram. The circuit has a 2-input AND gate with output Q. Its inputs are connected to a NOT gate with input B and output B2', and a 2-input OR gate with inputs B and B passed through a NOT gate with its output labeled B1'. The timing diagram initially has B=1, B1'=0, B+B1;=1, B2'=0, and Q=0 at time 0. Then B changes from 1 to 0, and at time 5, B2' changes from 0 to 1. At time 10, Q changs from 0 to 1. At time 15, B+B1' changes to 0, and at time 20, Q changes to 0. At time 25, B1' changes to 1. At time 40, B+B1' changes to 1. Finally, at time 45, Q changes to 1.␀)/K 27/P 38 0 R /Pg 18874 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
