<</A 28047 0 R /Alt(Figure 10.2: a?b?c: \(a\) Truth table; \(b\) Implementation using two cells of a PAL. The upper cell generates a'b'c+a'bc'+ab'c' and the lower cell generates the final function. There are two OR gates, each receiving inputs from three AND gates. In addition to a, b, c, d, and their complements, the AND gates can receive an input from the output of the upper OR gate or its complement. The upper or gate has a', b', and c input to its first AND gate, a', b, and c' input to its second AND gate, and a, b', and c input to its third AND gate. The lower OR gate has the output of the first OR gate input to its first AND gate, and a, b, and c input to its second AND gate. The third AND gate has no connections.␀)/K 0/P 39 0 R /Pg 18704 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
