<</A 28061 0 R /Alt(Figure 10.5: PLD model of an 8x2 ROM. There are eight AND gates, each of which can receive A2, A1, A0, and their complements as inputs. The outputs of the AND gates can be connected to two OR gates with outputs D1 and D0. The values of the A inputs and their complements determine the address of the location for each AND gate. For example, the upper AND gate has A2', A1', and A0' as its inputs; this gate represents address 000. These are the same for all ROMs of this size. The first OR gate has connections to the first, fourth, fifth, and sevents AND gates from the top. The second OR gate has connections to the first, second, fourth, and sixth AND gates from the top.␀)/K 10/P 39 0 R /Pg 18710 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
