<</A 28062 0 R /Alt(Figure 10.6: D flip-flop model of a 16x2 ROM. Buffer enable signals shown in green. A 4 to 16 decoder with inputs A3, A2, A1, and A0 outputs signals labeled O0 through O15. For each output Oi, there are two flip-flops labeled i1 and i0. The decoder output Oi enables two tri-state buffers, one connected to the output of each flip-flop i1 and i0. The outputs of all tri-state buffers labeled i1 are wired together and connect to output D1. Similarly, the outputs of all tri-state buffers labeled i0 are wired together and connect to output D0.␀)/K 10/P 39 0 R /Pg 18711 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
endobj
