<</A 28074 0 R /Alt(Figure 10.9: D flip-flop model of a 16x2 ROM with chip enable and output enable signals. This is the same as the previous figure, with tri-state buffers added to the lines that generate D1 and D0. The signals Chip Enable and Output Enable are input to an AND gate; the output of this gate enables these two additional tri-state buffers. Chip Enable is also connected to the Enable signal of the two decoders.␀)/K 16/P 39 0 R /Pg 18714 0 R /S/Figure/T()>>
